       "etitle": "Manual lane-change indicator (trial)",
-      "edescr": "At 5km/h or above, same-direction steering is confirmed for 0.15s. Release or brief countersteer does not erase continued boundary approach: recent intent is retained for up to 1.5s. Approach stopping for over 0.3s, retreat exceeding 0.15m for 0.15s or a four-second episode limit cancels tracking. On the left, fresh OEM white-line classification excludes centre lines; yellow, unknown or stale classifications block requests. On the right, road-edge clearance beyond the approached boundary must be at least 2.5m both nearby and ahead. Outer-line probability, adjacent lane width and road-edge standard deviation are not admission conditions. A wide shoulder can also pass the distance condition. Independent of ATC and the right-turn distance option; never requests automatic steering. Default OFF; Ioniq 5 PE with Jetson USB2CAN and AutoBlinkerControl 1 or 2 only. New requests need three seconds and one second of lamp extinction; steering-feedback isolation remains at least 12 seconds. Detection does not guarantee a real lane or safe gap. Revised behavior needs physical validation. Entry anchors target-line confidence of at least 10%; continuous approach may then be tracked for up to four seconds. After requesting, tracks completion, return or invalid inputs for at most 12 seconds. Immediate extinction of OEM one-touch flashing is not guaranteed. Measured boundary approach projects 0.3 seconds ahead to request indication earlier. The centre-to-boundary distance threshold advances from 0.9m to at most 1.2m; at least 0.15m of actual approach, driver intent and consistent movement of both boundaries remain required. Boundary retreat must persist for 0.15s to cancel tracking, and new indications pause during retreat. Recent steering intent and paired boundary movement with consistent lane width permit bounded position changes during approach. With a continuous target boundary and recent driver intent, a brief jump of the opposite boundary can wait up to 0.15s for valid samples. New indication pauses during the gap and requires consistent movement of both boundaries afterward.\nThe supported Panda/SPAS output uses these same settings and decisions. It is available on IONIQ 5 PE, IONIQ 9 and Azera / Grandeur GN7 with camera-SCC CAN-FD.\nFor manual lane changes and turns, normal completion waits for a minimum of two seconds from the first Panda/SPAS transmission request. Physical lever input, cancellation and input or lane errors end the request immediately. Actual flash count depends on the vehicle.\nAn invalid lane width pauses new approach admission. An established approach can continue when valid geometry returns within 0.15s of its last valid sample. Lane admission for a manual crossing is decided by the detector. The output stage checks request freshness, vehicle state and driver cancellation.",
+      "edescr": "At 5km/h or above, same-direction steering is confirmed for 0.15s. Release or brief countersteer does not erase continued boundary approach: recent intent is retained for up to 1.5s. Approach stopping for over 0.3s, retreat exceeding 0.15m for 0.15s or a four-second episode limit cancels tracking. On the left, fresh OEM white-line classification excludes centre lines; yellow, unknown or stale classifications block requests. On the right, road-edge clearance beyond the approached boundary must be at least 2.5m both nearby and ahead. Outer-line probability, adjacent lane width and road-edge standard deviation are not admission conditions. A wide shoulder can also pass the distance condition. Independent of ATC and the right-turn distance option; never requests automatic steering. Default OFF; protocol-matched USB2CAN, BLE or Panda/SPAS outputs and AutoBlinkerControl 1 or 2 only. New requests need three seconds and one second of lamp extinction; steering-feedback isolation remains at least 12 seconds. Detection does not guarantee a real lane or safe gap. Revised behavior needs physical validation. Entry anchors target-line confidence of at least 10%; continuous approach may then be tracked for up to four seconds. After requesting, tracks completion, return or invalid inputs for at most 12 seconds. Immediate extinction of OEM one-touch flashing is not guaranteed. Measured boundary approach projects 0.3 seconds ahead to request indication earlier. The centre-to-boundary distance threshold advances from 0.9m to at most 1.2m; at least 0.15m of actual approach, driver intent and consistent movement of both boundaries remain required. Boundary retreat must persist for 0.15s to cancel tracking, and new indications pause during retreat. Recent steering intent and paired boundary movement with consistent lane width permit bounded position changes during approach. With a continuous target boundary and recent driver intent, a brief jump of the opposite boundary can wait up to 0.15s for valid samples. New indication pauses during the gap and requires consistent movement of both boundaries afterward.\nThe supported Panda/SPAS output uses these same settings and decisions. It is available on camera-SCC CAN-FD with ECAN SPAS 0x165 (24 bytes), 0x16A (32 bytes) and stalk 0x3C1 (8 bytes), without a model-name restriction.\nFor manual lane changes and turns, normal completion waits for a minimum of two seconds from the first Panda/SPAS transmission request. Physical lever input, cancellation and input or lane errors end the request immediately. Actual flash count depends on the vehicle.\nAn invalid lane width pauses new approach admission. An established approach can continue when valid geometry returns within 0.15s of its last valid sample. Lane admission for a manual crossing is decided by the detector. The output stage checks request freshness, vehicle state and driver cancellation.\nAn early boundary fluctuation is checked only within an existing request. Near-edge paired lane reassignment can wait 0.15s. When an uncertain target boundary retreats but the opposite boundary and driver steering support continued approach, stable lane geometry must return within three seconds. Opposite driver steering and invalid inputs still cancel.",
       "cgroup": "转向设置",
       "ctitle": "手动变道转向灯（试验）",
-      "cdescr": "车速至少5km/h，确认同方向转向0.15秒后，松手或短暂反向施力但仍接近边界时最多保留意图1.5秒；停止接近超过0.3秒、回退超过0.15米且持续0.15秒或单次跟踪超过4秒则取消。左侧通过新鲜的原车白线分类排除中央线，黄色、未知或过期分类阻止触发。右侧仅要求当前及前方的目标车道线至道路边缘距离至少2.5米；不使用外侧车道线概率、相邻车道宽度或道路边缘标准差。宽路肩也可能满足距离条件。 独立于ATC及右转距离选项，不请求自动转向。默认关闭，仅支持Ioniq 5 PE、Jetson USB2CAN及自动转向灯模式1或2。再次请求须间隔3秒且连续熄灯1秒，自动转向反馈隔离至少12秒。不能保证真实车道或安全间距，修改后仍需实车验证。 开始接近时确认目标线置信度至少10%，连续接近最多跟踪4秒。请求后跟踪完成、返回或输入失效，最长12秒；不能保证原车轻触闪灯立即熄灭。 根据测得的车道边界接近速度预测0.3秒后的位置，提前请求转向灯。车体中心至边界的距离阈值从0.9米最多提前至1.2米，仍要求至少0.15米实际接近、驾驶员意图及两侧边界一致移动。 边界回退持续0.15秒才取消跟踪，回退期间暂停新请求。近期转向意图及两侧边界同向移动、车道宽度一致时，允许有限的位置变化并继续跟踪。 目标边界连续且近期有驾驶员转向意图时，对侧边界短暂跳变可等待最多0.15秒恢复有效观测。等待期间暂停新指示，恢复后仍须两侧边界移动一致。\n支持的Panda/SPAS输出使用相同设置和判断，适用于摄像头SCC CAN-FD配置的IONIQ 5 PE、IONIQ 9和Grandeur GN7。\n手动变道和转弯正常提前完成时，Panda/SPAS从首次发送请求起至少保持2秒。实际拨杆操作、取消、输入或车道错误会立即结束请求。实际闪烁次数取决于车辆。\n车道宽度暂时无效时暂停新的接近判断。已建立的接近过程可在最后一次有效观测后的0.15秒内恢复有效几何时继续。手动变道请求的车道判断由检测器完成，输出阶段检查请求时效、车辆状态和驾驶员取消。",
