-      "edescr": "Detects driver turns using steering torque, wheel movement and measured vehicle rotation. Operates independently of ATC, including intersections with faint lane markings. Starts at 5–60km/h after 0.15s same-direction driver torque, at least 42 degrees steering with a 22-degree increase and consistent vehicle rotation. Ends after wheel return within ±15 degrees and settled rotation, opposite driver steering, or 30 seconds. Default OFF. Requires Ioniq 5 PE, a supported indicator adapter and AutoBlinkerControl 1 or 2. Parking-aisle turns can also trigger. Curves and evasive maneuvers can cause false indications. Physical lamp validation remains pending. When same-direction manual-turn conditions are met during a manual lane indication, the existing request continues under turn completion tracking. Lane-position jumps at junctions do not reset manual turns established through driver torque, increasing steering angle and measured rotation. An owned indication survives small negative speed-estimator noise around zero while standstill is confirmed in Drive.\nThe supported Panda/SPAS output uses these same settings and decisions. It is available on IONIQ 5 PE, IONIQ 9 and Azera / Grandeur GN7 with camera-SCC CAN-FD.\nFor manual lane changes and turns, normal completion waits for a minimum of two seconds from the first Panda/SPAS transmission request. Physical lever input, cancellation and input or lane errors end the request immediately. Actual flash count depends on the vehicle.",
+      "edescr": "Detects driver turns using steering torque, wheel movement and measured vehicle rotation. Operates independently of ATC, including intersections with faint lane markings. Starts at 5–60km/h after 0.15s same-direction driver torque, at least 42 degrees steering with a 22-degree increase and consistent vehicle rotation. Ends after wheel return within ±15 degrees and settled rotation, opposite driver steering, or 30 seconds. Default OFF. Requires a protocol-matched USB2CAN, BLE or Panda/SPAS adapter and AutoBlinkerControl 1 or 2. Parking-aisle turns can also trigger. Curves and evasive maneuvers can cause false indications. Physical lamp validation remains pending. When same-direction manual-turn conditions are met during a manual lane indication, the existing request continues under turn completion tracking. Lane-position jumps at junctions do not reset manual turns established through driver torque, increasing steering angle and measured rotation. An owned indication survives small negative speed-estimator noise around zero while standstill is confirmed in Drive.\nThe supported Panda/SPAS output uses these same settings and decisions. It is available on camera-SCC CAN-FD with ECAN SPAS 0x165 (24 bytes), 0x16A (32 bytes) and stalk 0x3C1 (8 bytes), without a model-name restriction.\nFor manual lane changes and turns, normal completion waits for a minimum of two seconds from the first Panda/SPAS transmission request. Physical lever input, cancellation and input or lane errors end the request immediately. Actual flash count depends on the vehicle.\nAfter opposite steering ends a manual turn, the next opposite turn can retain recent steering evidence at 10km/h or above. Only the last 0.25s before rearm bridges the angle reference; the existing two-second wait, one continuous dark second and current same-direction steering remain required. Retained intent expires after three seconds without resetting ordinary fresh-steering detection.",
